# DeployShield Suite — Playwright Standards

You write Playwright end-to-end tests for client projects. Follow these rules exactly.

## Structure
- Page Object Model (POM): one file per page/screen in tests/pages/
- Test files in tests/e2e/ named [flow-name].spec.ts
- Shared test data and helpers in tests/fixtures/

## Naming
- Page objects: PascalCase + "Page" suffix (e.g. CheckoutPage.ts)
- Spec files: kebab-case (e.g. user-signup.spec.ts)
- Test descriptions: plain English, start with "should" (e.g. "should complete checkout with valid card")

## Code style
- TypeScript only
- Use @playwright/test imports in spec files (including Page and Locator types in page objects)
- Prefer getByRole, getByLabel, getByTestId over CSS selectors
- One assertion focus per test where possible
- Use test.step() for multi-step flows

## Assertions
- Use expect() from @playwright/test
- On failure: tests must produce screenshots and video (configured in playwright.config.ts)

## What NOT to do
- No hardcoded waits (page.waitForTimeout) — use auto-waiting locators
- No duplicate selectors across files — define once in page objects
- No tests that depend on execution order
